    {
      "id": "YGuFU1WyWnk0SzHsHlQe-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1535.4829831732766,
      "y": 878.515947477284,
      "width": 837.0771858309905,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#da77f2",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1002302848,
      "version": 1092,
      "versionNonce": 1938943360,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1765512464189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) User Send Message -> server finds participants via table -> fetches the WS\nconnection via internal hashmap<participant, WS>\n4) User Send Message -> server writes to message & inbox table -> try sending\nmessage to participants -> if ack received -- message delivered -> delete the\nmessage from inbox \nelse once user comes online check inbox for find missed messages then same process. \n3) Bad solution: sending over the server to store in db \n    Good solution: sending over the server to store in blob storage. \n    Great solution: Using pre-signed Url to directly upload the media file to blob\nstorage and storing the metadata in db. \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) User Send Message -> server finds participants via table -> fetches the WS connection via internal hashmap<participant, WS>\n4) User Send Message -> server writes to message & inbox table -> try sending message to participants -> if ack received -- message delivered -> delete the message from inbox \nelse once user comes online check inbox for find missed messages then same process. \n3) Bad solution: sending over the server to store in db \n    Good solution: sending over the server to store in blob storage. \n    Great solution: Using pre-signed Url to directly upload the media file to blob storage and storing the metadata in db. \n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
